# Modularization by Responsibility

Modularize code by functional responsibility, not by file length.

When creating or refactoring code:

* Extract code only when it represents a distinct responsibility, reusable behavior, business logic, or architectural boundary.
* Do not split a file solely because it is large.
* Avoid unnecessary layers, wrappers, services, helpers, or files.
* Prefer extending an existing appropriate module before creating a new one.
* Keep related logic together when separation would make the code harder to understand or navigate.

Prefer the simplest structure that keeps responsibilities clear.
